commit e3e91ede09f908184c4fcb6f07a77f42b52af1f6

C03: quoted or dictated clipboard literals reach clipboard.write.text; clipboard reads and writes are reviewed turns (CLIPBOARD1359)

The three clipboard literals of the registry never reached an operation: «Copia a mi portapapeles "Hola"» and «copiá esto al portapapeles: hola mundo» resolved to nothing (the write reader only vetoed vocabulary and had no literal grounding), and «qué hay en el portapapeles» resolved to clipboard.read.text without grounded arguments. Both operations are PrivacySensitive, so the product asks for confirmation and the conductor's reviewed turn had no admission for them.

effect_intent.literal_clipboard_write_text: a copy/put head, the clipboard named and a literal that is either quoted («"Hola"», «“…”», ««…»») or introduced by a colon after the clipboard noun; case and accents preserved; no literal or a prohibition → None (the «este texto» clarification stays). resolve_explicit_effects proposes clipboard.write.text with the raw text as evidence.
__main__._explicit_arguments_from_evidence: clipboard.write.text → {"text": literal}; clipboard.read.text → {} when the clipboard is named.
Baxy.App ProductConductorHost: turn.confirm-reviewed also admits clipboard.write.text and clipboard.read.text proposals (root approves only the exact literal / an argument-free read).

Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order). App recompiled in BUILD1359.

